<h3 id=3D"view-types">View types</h3>

<p>Prefer view types (e.g., <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-r=
ouge">std::string_view</code>, <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighte=
r-rouge">std::Span&lt;T&gt;</code>,
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">absl::FunctionRef&lt;R=
(Args...)&gt;</code>) for function arguments (unless ownership of the
data is being transferred). These types reduce copying, and allow callers t=
o
pick their own container types (e.g., one caller might use <code class=3D"l=
anguage-plaintext highlighter-rouge">std::vector</code> whereas
another one uses <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">absl:=
:InlinedVector</code>).</p>

<h3 id=3D"pre-allocatedpre-computed-arguments">Pre-allocated/pre-computed a=
rguments</h3>

<p>For frequently called routines, sometimes it is useful to allow higher-l=
evel
callers to pass in a data structure that they own or information that the c=
alled
routine needs that the client already has. This can avoid the low-level rou=
tine
being forced to allocate its own temporary data structure or recompute
already-available information.</p>

