<h3 id=3D"simd-instructions">SIMD Instructions</h3>

<p>Explore whether handling multiple items at once using
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_instruction,_multiple_data"=
>SIMD</a>
instructions available on modern CPUs can give speedups (e.g., see
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">absl::flat_hash_map</c=
ode> discussion below in <a href=3D"https://abseil.io/fast/hints.html#bulk-=
operations">Bulk Operations</a>
section).</p>

<h3 id=3D"reduce-false-sharing">Reduce false sharing</h3>

<p>If different threads access different mutable data, consider placing the
different data items on different cache lines, e.g., in C++ using the <code=
 class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">alignas</code>
directive. However, these directives are easy to misuse and may increase ob=
ject
sizes significantly, so make sure performance measurements justify their us=
e.</p>

<details class=3D"zippy">
<summary><p>Segregate commonly mutated fields in a different cache
line than other fields.</p>
</summary>

<p>histogram.h</p>

<div class=3D"old">
<pre><code class=3D"language-c++">HistogramOptions options_;
...
internal::HistogramBoundaries *boundaries_;
...
std::vector&lt;double&gt; buckets_;

double min_;             // Minimum.
double max_;             // Maximum.
double count_;           // Total count of occurrences.
double sum_;             // Sum of values.
double sum_of_squares_;  // Sum of squares of values.
...
RegisterVariableExporter *exporter_;
</code></pre>
</div>

<div class=3D"new">
<pre><code class=3D"language-c++">  HistogramOptions options_;
  ...
  internal::HistogramBoundaries *boundaries_;
  ...
  RegisterVariableExporter *exporter_;
  ...
  // Place the following fields in a dedicated cacheline as they are freque=
ntly
  // mutated, so we can avoid potential false sharing.
  ...
#ifndef SWIG
  alignas(ABSL_CACHELINE_SIZE)
#endif
