<details class=3D"zippy">
<summary><p>Decode four integers at a time (circa 2004).</p>
</summary>

<p>Introduced a
<a href=3D"https://static.googleusercontent.com/media/research.google.com/e=
n//people/jeff/WSDM09-keynote.pdf">GroupVarInt format</a>
that encodes/decodes groups of 4 variable-length integers at a time in 5-17
bytes, rather than one integer at a time. Decoding one group of 4 integers =
in
the new format takes ~1/3rd the time of decoding 4 individually varint-enco=
ded
integers.</p>
<p>groupvarint.cc</p>

<div class=3D"new">
<pre><code class=3D"language-c++">const char* DecodeGroupVar(const char* p,=
 int N, uint32* dest) {
  assert(groupvar_initialized);
  assert(N % 4 =3D=3D 0);
  while (N) {
    uint8 tag =3D *p;
    p++;

    uint8* lenptr =3D &amp;groupvar_table[tag].length[0];

#define GET_NEXT                                        \
    do {                                                \
      uint8 len =3D *lenptr;                              \
      *dest =3D UNALIGNED_LOAD32(p) &amp; groupvar_mask[len]; \
      dest++;                                           \
      p +=3D len;                                         \
      lenptr++;                                         \
    } while (0)
    GET_NEXT;
    GET_NEXT;
    GET_NEXT;
    GET_NEXT;
#undef GET_NEXT

    N -=3D 4;
  }
  return p;
}
</code></pre>
</div>


</details>

